  "notes": "{慣|な}らす is a godan verb meaning \"to accustom\" or \"to train\"—to make something or someone familiar with a condition.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{慣|な}れる→慣れる：00870_nareru⟧ (intransitive, to get used to)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧〜⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{慣|な}らす: to accustom ~ to ~\n- ⟦{体|からだ}→体：00784_karada⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{寒|さむ}さ→寒さ：12336_samusa⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{慣|な}らす: to accustom one's body to cold\n- ⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{暗|くら}さ→暗い：00647_kurai⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{慣|な}らす: to let one's eyes adjust to darkness\n- ⟦{靴|くつ}→靴：00725_kutsu⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{慣|な}らす: to break in shoes\n\nHOMOPHONES (different kanji):\n- ⟦{鳴|な}らす→鳴らす：02381_narasu⟧: to ring, to sound\n- {均|な}らす: to level, to even out\n- {馴|な}らす: alternative writing for \"to tame\"",
